<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Addis Ababa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1896</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-italo-ethiopian-war">First Italo-Ethiopian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a> was signed in 1896 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> after the Ethiopian victory at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adwa">Battle of Adwa</a>. It annulled the disputed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-wuchale">Treaty of Wuchale</a> and recognised Ethiopia's full independence. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> profile treats it as the diplomatic confirmation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a>'s military triumph, which made Ethiopia one of the few African states to avoid European colonisation.</p></div>
